ID  - P2-0016
TI  - A Review of BIM-GIS and Sensor Data Fusion for Predictive Maintenance in Infrastructure
AU  - Lai, Yuqu
PY  - 2026
JO  - Advances in Engineering Technology Research
DO  - 10.56028/aetr.16.1.567.2026
UR  - https://consensus.app/papers/a-review-of-bimgis-and-sensor-data-fusion-for-predictive-lai/8b561bf257485321bb9b03946f36234a/
AB  - As urban construction shifts from reactive protection to proactive preventive maintenance, traditional static BIM-GIS platforms struggle to meet demands for infrastructure health monitoring and hazard diagnosis throughout the entire lifecycle. This paper addresses the core challenge of effectively integrating real-time sensor data with static BIM-GIS models to construct a digital twin framework that supports infrastructure predictive maintenance through a systematic review. The paper first analyzes the data requirements for infrastructure predictive maintenance, focusing on the “sensing-transmission-analysis-integration” technology chain. It then demonstrates, through applications such as early health warnings and operational health monitoring in bridges, roads, and public facilities, that this integrated technology significantly enhances maintenance efficiency and reduces operational costs. Finally, it analyzes current research challenges, including data standardization, real-time computational efficiency, and multilingual adaptability, while outlining future trends integrating AI and "cloud-edge-terminal" collaborative computing.
