ID  - P2-0055
TI  - Big Data and Blockchain-Based Engineering Management Platform
AU  - Chen, Hang
AU  - Liu, Chunling
AU  - Shen, Hao
AU  - Qiang, Liao
AU  - Hui, Liu
AU  - Peng, Xu
PY  - 2026
JO  - Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Digital Management and Information Technology
DO  - 10.1145/3808707.3808796
UR  - https://consensus.app/papers/big-data-and-blockchainbased-engineering-management-chen-liu/bcdd8c6a6e615301ac5278c9ef52dbfa/
AB  - Construction quality management requires multi-stakeholder coordination across material acceptance, process inspection, concealed-work acceptance, testing, and corrective-action closure. In practice, heterogeneous data sources, long handoff chains, and unclear accountability boundaries make quality data hard to trace, verify, share across organizations, and audit for regulatory purposes. This paper presents an engineering-deployable digital quality management platform that integrates a consortium blockchain with an event-driven big-data pipeline. A dual-layer trust model is adopted: only fingerprints, signatures, and linkage indices are anchored on-chain, while detailed records and multimedia evidence are retained off-chain. Smart-contract state machines enforce prerequisite checks and endorsement accountability for key workflows (materials, inspections, tests, and nonconformance reports), and on-chain events trigger off-chain batch-stream fusion analytics for minute-level risk aggregation and alerting. A prototype implementation is evaluated on four end-to-end scenarios and shows that second-level evidence anchoring and minute-level risk dashboard refresh can be achieved under fine-grained access control, improving trust, sharing efficiency, and auditability.
