ID  - P2-0200
TI  - xpSHACL: Explainable SHACL Validation using Retrieval-Augmented Generation and Large Language Models
AU  - G. Publio
AU  - J. E. L. Gayo
PY  - 2025
JO  - ArXiv
VL  - abs/2507.08432
DO  - 10.48550/arxiv.2507.08432
UR  - https://consensus.app/papers/xpshacl-explainable-shacl-validation-using-publio-gayo/9dc9f794e3405ae1b9bb212746eefdab/
AB  - Shapes Constraint Language (SHACL) is a powerful language for validating RDF data. Given the recent industry attention to Knowledge Graphs (KGs), more users need to validate linked data properly. However, traditional SHACL validation engines often provide terse reports in English that are difficult for non-technical users to interpret and act upon. This paper presents xpSHACL, an explainable SHACL validation system that addresses this issue by combining rule-based justification trees with retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) and large language models (LLMs) to produce detailed, multilanguage, human-readable explanations for constraint violations. A key feature of xpSHACL is its usage of a Violation KG to cache and reuse explanations, improving efficiency and consistency.
